      "text": "We begin by analyzing the given diagram and the angles involved. The problem states that \\( RSP \\) is a straight line and that \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\). We need to find the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\).\n\nFirst, let's determine the measure of \\(\\angle QRS\\). Since \\( RSP \\) is a straight line, the angles \\(\\angle RQS\\) and \\(\\angle SQR\\) are supplementary. Therefore, the sum of these two angles is \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\n\\]\n\nWe know that:\n\\[\n\\angle QRP = 80^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThis implies that:\n\\[\n\\angle QSR = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\(\\angle PQR\\). Notice that \\(\\angle PQR\\) is part of the straight line \\(RSP\\). The angle \\(\\angle PQR\\) can be found by subtracting \\(\\angle QRS\\) from \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\nSince \\(\\angle QRS = 100^\\circ\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\angle PQR = 180^\\circ - 100^\\circ = 80^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{80}\n\\]",
