      "text": "To find the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\), we start by analyzing the given information and the geometric relationships in the diagram.\n\n1. **Identify the given angle:**\n   \\[\n   \\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n2. **Understand the nature of the angles:**\n   - \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, which means \\(\\angle PRS + \\angle SQT = 180^\\circ\\). However, we are not directly concerned with \\(\\angle PRS\\) or \\(\\angle SQT\\) in the calculation of \\(\\angle PQR\\).\n\n3. **Focus on \\(\\angle PQR\\):**\n   - \\(\\angle PQR\\) is part of the straight line \\(RSP\\).\n   - The angle \\(\\angle SPQ\\) (which is the exterior angle to \\(\\angle PQR\\)) is given as \\(80^\\circ\\).\n\n4. **Calculate \\(\\angle PQR\\):**\n   - Since \\(\\angle PQR\\) and \\(\\angle SPQ\\) are supplementary (they form a straight line), we have:\n     \\[\n     \\angle PQR + \\angle SPQ = 180^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - Substituting the given value of \\(\\angle SPQ\\):\n     \\[\n     \\angle PQR + 80^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - Solving for \\(\\angle PQR\\):\n     \\[\n     \\angle PQR = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{100}\\).",
